<div class="wp-block-group alignfull has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained" style="padding-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)"><h1 class="wp-block-post-title">Download</h1>

<div class="entry-content alignfull wp-block-post-content has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-post-content-is-layout-constrained">
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Versions</h2>



<p>The SHL dataset is released progressively as it is prepared.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>SHL Preview: 3 users, 3 days per users, including 4 phone locations and timelapse camera.</li>



<li>SHL Complete User 1 â€“ Hips phone: 1 user, all the recording days (about 7 months), comprising only the phone placed at the pocket (Hips) and timelapse camera. This is the part of the dataset used for the the 2018 SHL Challenge.</li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">License</h2>



<p>This dataset is made publicly available solely for non-profit and research purposes. For any other usage, please contact daniel.roggen@ieee.org to discuss licensing terms.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Citation request</h3>



<p>If you use the dataset, please cite at least:</p>



<p>[1] H. Gjoreski, M. Ciliberto, L. Wang, F. J. O. Morales, S. Mekki, S. Valentin, D. Roggen. <em>â€œThe University of Sussex-Huawei Locomotion and Transportation Dataset for Multimodal Analytics with Mobile Devices.â€</em> IEEE Access 6 (2018): 42592-42604.</p>



<p>[2] L. Wang, H. Gjoreski, M. Ciliberto, S. Mekki, S. Valentin, and D. Roggen, â€œ<em>Enabling reproducible research in sensor-based transportation mode recognition with the Sussex-Huawei dataset</em>,â€ IEEE Access 7 (2019): 10870-10891.</p>



<p>If you use the App, please cite at least:</p>



<p>[1] M. Ciliberto, F. J. OrdoÃ±ez Morales, H. Gjoreski, D. Roggen, S.Mekki, S.Valentin. <em>â€œHigh reliability Android application for multidevice multimodal mobile data acquisition and annotation.â€</em> In <em>Proc. ACM Conference on Embedded Networked Sensor Systems</em>. ACM, 2017.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Dataset naming</h3>



<p>We recommend to refer to the dataset as follows in your publications:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Use at least once the complete name: â€œ<em>The University of Sussex-Huawei Locomotion and Transportation Dataset</em>â€ or â€œ<em>The Sussex-Huawei Locomotion and Transportation Dataset</em>â€œ. You may introduce the acronym of the dataset as well: â€œ<em>The University of Sussex-Huawei Locomotion-Transportation (SHL) Dataset</em>â€œ.</li>



<li>Subsequently, you may refer to the dataset with its acronym: â€œ<em>The SHL Dataset</em>â€œ.</li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Dataset documentation</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20241212152116/http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/11/doc_dataset.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Data organisation and file formats</a> (30.11.2017)</li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">SHL Dataset â€“ Preview</h2>



<p>This release comprises a part of the complete dataset. It includes:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Data from all three users and all four phone locations</li>



<li>Three recording-days per user</li>



<li>59 hours of annotated recordings, corresponding to 227 hours of data for the 4 phone locations</li>



<li>All sensor modalities, except for audio</li>
</ul>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full is-resized" id="attachment_741"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="768" height="576" src="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/SHLDataset_preview_map-768x576-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-1608" style="width:1100px;height:auto"><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Trajectories covered by the users in the SHL Preview dataset</figcaption></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full" id="attachment_740"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="384" src="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/SHLDataset_preview_actlen-1024x384-1.png" alt="" class="wp-image-1607"><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Distributions of the activities in the SHL Preview dataset</figcaption></figure>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Release history</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Version 1 (3 November 2017): initial release</li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Download</h3>



<p>Due to size, the download is split in 3 parts. Part 1 contains the data of user 1 and Matlab demonstration scripts. Part 2 and 3 contain the data of user 2 and 3 respectively.</p>



<p>Version 1 as zip: <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/release_SHLDataset_preview_v1/SHLDataset_preview_v1_part1.zip">Part 1 (2.7GB)</a>, <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/release_SHLDataset_preview_v1/SHLDataset_preview_v1_part2.zip">Part 2 (2.3GB)</a>, <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/release_SHLDataset_preview_v1/SHLDataset_preview_v1_part3.zip">Part 3 (2.1GB)</a></p>



<p>Version 1 as tarball (tar.gz): <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/release_SHLDataset_preview_v1/SHLDataset_preview_v1_part1.tar.gz">Part 1 (3.7GB)</a>, <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/release_SHLDataset_preview_v1/SHLDataset_preview_v1_part2.tar.gz">Part2 (3.2GB)</a>, <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/release_SHLDataset_preview_v1/SHLDataset_preview_v1_part3.tar.gz">Part 3 (2.9GB)</a></p>



<p>Notes:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Please use 7zip to extract the ZIP files.</li>



<li>A solution to the VideoReader error in MATLAB under Linux can be found <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20241212152116/https://uk.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/answers/94531-why-do-i-receive-an-error-when-creating-a-videoreader-object-on-linux-in-matlab-r2010b-7-11" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">here</a></li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">SHL Dataset â€“ Complete User 1 â€“ Hips Phone</h2>



<p>This release comprises a much larger part of the SHL dataset than the SHL Preview. It contains the original data which was used in the 2018 SHL Challenge. This release comprises:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Data from one user (User 1).</li>



<li>Data from one phone only, placed in trousers front pocket (Hips).</li>



<li>391 hours of recordings over 7 months.</li>



<li>All sensor modalities (including timelapse video), except for audio.</li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Download</h3>



<p>Due to size, the download is split in multiple parts. Download all the parts in the same folder.</p>



<p>Use 7zip to extract the files from the archive: 7z x SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.001</p>



<p><a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.001">SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.001</a>; <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.002">SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.002</a>; <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.003">SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.003</a>; <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.004">SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.004</a>; <a href="http://www.shl-dataset.org/wp-content/uploads/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2/SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.005">SHLDataset_User1Hips_v2.zip.005</a></p>
